(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609161900-kotoba-uiux-behavior-layer-theme-defaults-closing")
  (:adr/title "kotoba UI/UX 2026-09-16: the headless behavior layer for DADS, wrappers for all 40 components, the full --hig-* contract, cloud-kotoba-dds.theme as the default tokens of every Kotoba app, kotoba.cloud on it through the shinkansen theme contract, docs.kotoba.cloud/graph/ repaired — session closing")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-16")
  (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2609160130" "ADR-2609151708" "ADR-2608080100" "ADR-2608260900" "ADR-2608136000" "ADR-2609112300" "ADR-2607141915"))
  (:adr/context
  "One session, five owner asks in order. (1) 'docs.kotoba.cloud/graph/ の uiux が崩れている。原因は? cloud-kotoba-dds, shinkansen は適切に利用できている?' (2) 'ok, do it' on the four-step fix. (3) 'shadcn/ui, radix のような component, design token の充実度はどうなっている?' (4) 'do it' on the four-step gap plan (behavior layer, the 26 wrappers, token unification, sheet/composer). (5) mid-turn: 'kotoba.cloud の uiux を app.itonami.cloud の uiux token に合わせてほしい。app.itonami.cloud の uiux, design token を cloud-kotoba-dds のデフォルトとしてほしい. shinkansen webframework を使ってほしい'.

  Measured before touching anything. /docs/graph/: the live body was byte-identical to the origin/main render; graph-docs-html (written 2026-09-14, #97) hand-built page/page with the marketing site-header/site-footer and inlined only skin + bridge + shell CSS, so 27 of its 54 class names (kc-header, kc-nav, kc-footer, kc-skip, kc-wordmark, kc-legal__lead …) had no rule — the header a bare list of links, the skip link in view, no docs map, light only — and shinkansen.audit scored it 98.3 because no axis asked whether a class the document names has a rule. Two more defects on the same path: every docs URL without its trailing slash 307-ed to the apex-form path on the docs host (/graph → /docs/graph/ → 404), and the header's Blog entry was an empty <a> in every locale.

  The stack against shadcn/Radix (jp-go-dds bcf5262 / cloud-kotoba-dds e69e78b / shinkansen a79c874, all origin/main): DADS vendored CSS 40 components, hiccup wrappers 20 (14 DADS + 6 dds-ext layout), behaviour scripts 2 (language selector, theme toggle) plus 5 pattern-specific scripts in cloud-kotoba-dds — no headless layer at all; DADS custom properties 187 (colour primitives 130, neutral 26, key 13, semantic 8, elevation 8, font-family 2 — no spacing / radius / type-size tokens upstream) and the --hig-* bridge 71; cloud-kotoba-dds 11 namespaces / ≈70 app-pattern fns; shinkansen 18 namespaces of which app-kotoba-cloud required 2 (audit, coscientist); jp-go-dds consumed by 616 deps.edn, cloud-kotoba-dds by 3, shinkansen by 1.

  app.itonami.cloud (network-awai/cloud-itonami, the legacy kotoba-ui stack with a jp-go-dds bridge on top): in Chrome its --hig-* computed to the bridge's values — DADS key blue #0017c1, DADS neutrals, Noto Sans JP, rem-calc spacing — the same values kotoba.cloud resolved; it DECLARED 117 --hig-* where kotoba.cloud declared 71, the 46 apart being the 11 text styles' font-weight / font-family, display1-3 (5 each) and the six palette members (teal / mint / indigo / brown / gray2-6) that the bridge had left to a shitsuke.hig layer DADS-based apps do not have (they resolved to nothing). Its body: rgb(242,242,242), 17px / 22px, box-sizing border-box; kotoba.cloud's: white, 16px, line-height normal.")
  (:adr/decision
  "1. docs.kotoba.cloud/graph/ is a docs-page over docs-site/graph-view (the shell, the docs map, /css/site.css, dark); graph-docs-view and the hand-built head are gone. site-css carries cloud-kotoba-dds.catalog/css — eight catalog pages had named it in :extra-css and site-layout dropped the key; :extra-css is a checked declaration now (a vector the render asserts site-css carries, throwing otherwise). worker.cljk directory-redirect answers the trailing slash on docs.kotoba.cloud and kyber.kotoba.cloud itself. Blog label restored. app-kotoba-cloud 4639f5cb (PR #259), deployed ef3bb341.

  2. shinkansen.audit gains :classes-styled (d1a3ca3, PR #4): the share of class names the body uses that a selector in the shipped CSS names; tolerance a fifth and at least one (healthy pages measure 3/58, 10/122 rule-less hook classes), linear to 0 at three fifths, :not-applicable without classes, :unmeasured when a referenced stylesheet is not supplied. Against the old /graph/ 0.21 with the 27 names; the app's audit script (hard axis) exits 1 on the old render, 0 on the new.

  3. jp-go-dds.behavior (9fd79a8 PR #10, 4a315c5 PR #11): ONE dependency-free, idempotent runtime keyed by data-behavior markers — dialog (the platform's <dialog> trap / Escape / focus return, plus the command/commandfor invoker polyfill and data-dialog-open/-close), menu ([data-menu-opener][aria-expanded] + [data-menu-popup][data-chrome=float]: click / ArrowDown open, Escape to the opener, outside click / focus close, Arrow / Home / End / typeahead, focus({preventScroll:true}) so an overflow container does not scroll), tabs (automatic activation, roving tabindex, orientation), disclosure, radiogroup (arrows move AND choose by clicking), toast (live region + jpGoDds.behavior.toast), combobox (filter, aria-activedescendant, Enter into a hidden input). behavior/css carries the layer rules on --hig-z-*; behavior/markers is data. Class names are never selected — markers only, the way :chrome-layers reads data-chrome.

  4. jp-go-dds.core wraps the 26 vendored components that had none, after the upstream example HTML at 3b34f4c (blockquote, breadcrumb, calendar as a static month grid from Sakamoto's day-of-week, carousel-single, date-picker separated, description-list, disclosure, drawer, emergency-banner, file-upload static, hamburger-menu-button, horizontal-menu, image, link, list, menu-list, menu-list-box, modal-dialog, page-navigation, progress-indicator, resource-list, search-box, step-navigation, tab, toc, utility-link), the script-driven ones carrying the marker; plus combobox / toast-region / toast as dds-ext. Where upstream's script is an application (calendar 14KB, carousel 9KB, file-upload 19KB) the wrapper emits the static view and its docstring says so.

  5. jp-go-dds.tokens bridge 71 → 128: the text styles' weight / family, display1-3 as fluid clamps, the six palette members as the nearest DADS primitives (teal cyan-600, mint cyan-400, indigo purple-600, brown orange-1000, gray2-6 neutral 420/300/200/100/50), and --hig-motion-press/-reveal/-panel (100/180/240ms), --hig-z-raised/-sticky/-float/-modal/-toast (1/20/40/60/80), --hig-breakpoint-xs/-sm/-md (480/640/960px) with tokens/motion, tokens/layers, tokens/breakpoints as data pinned equal by tokens_test. Custom properties cannot drive @media; the bands document the numbers the media rules state.

  6. shinkansen.audit gains :behaviors-delivered (8029db9, PR #6): a data-behavior marker must be selected by a shipped script (inline, or ctx :scripts resolved like :stylesheets) AND its subtree must carry what behavior-contract lists (menu: opener with aria-expanded + aria-controls, popup with data-chrome=float; tabs: tablist / tab[aria-selected] / tabpanel; combobox: the three aria on role=combobox + a listbox; dialog: <dialog> + aria-labelledby; toast: role=status + aria-live; radiogroup: role=radiogroup + radio[aria-checked]; disclosure: aria-expanded + aria-controls). The walker records :ancestors for subtree reads. And a bug the first multi-line inline script exposed (b1ac87a, PR #7): ClojureScript's string/replace rebuilds the RegExp keeping only g/i/m/u, so a dotall (?s).*? stopped matching across a newline in strip-opaque while re-find with the same literal still matched — script and style bodies with a newline were walked as markup. [\\s\\S]*? everywhere, with a test that fails on the old source.

  7. cloud-kotoba-dds.theme (80ad97b, PR #19) is the default of every Kotoba app: tokens = the 128-entry bridge (app.itonami.cloud's 117 are a subset resolving to the same values — the alignment the owner asked for is the contract, not a second palette), chrome-css = itonami's document defaults (box-sizing border-box, body on --hig-color-system-grouped-background in --hig-font-text at the body size / line-height, focus ring --hig-color-tint, controls inherit, reduced-motion), css in cascade order (skin → --ck-* layer → chrome → behavior → shell → switch → menu → status → sheet → code → console → catalog), stylesheet (dds + jp-go-dds.dark mirror + css), scripts (theme.js = shinkansen.theme/head-script, shinkansen.js = interaction/runtime, behavior.js, shell.js, switch.js, menu.js, status.js), head. Light / dark / system is the shinkansen contract, default system. theme_test pins contracts.edn :motion = tokens/motion and shinkansen.viewport/breakpoints = tokens/breakpoints. The shell's account entry is a behavior menu (button chip, role=menu / menuitem, up placement on the rail; shell/script only fills and reveals), the theme switch is a behavior radiogroup, the settings sheet of contracts.edn is a component (cloud-kotoba-dds.sheet: modal-dialog + bottom sheet below --hig-breakpoint-sm), console's one hex literal is a token. A parallel session's tokens / menu / status (PR #18) merged in; --ck-layer-top / --ck-layer-float / --ck-motion read --hig-z-sticky / --hig-z-float / --hig-motion-reveal instead of restating 20 / 80 / .16s.

  8. kotoba.cloud (app-kotoba-cloud 312f20bf, PR #271, deployed ae503a4f): site-css and the landing / legal inline css start from cloud-kotoba-dds.theme; the λ toggle is replaced by cloud-kotoba-dds.switch/theme-switch on shinkansen.theme (same storage key kotoba-theme and data-theme attribute, so a stored choice carries over); /js/theme.js, /js/shinkansen.js, /js/behavior.js, /js/switch.js, /js/menu.js, /js/status.js ship on every document; four console copy keys (theme / light / dark / system) authored en / ja and machine-translated for the other 20 locales; on the phone band the switch is compact and the top bar's section label — which repeated the h1 right under it — is gone (h1 at 217px on 390, floor 240; 269 with the switch alone). uiux-audit supplies ctx :scripts and :actions {:events {}}; classes-styled and behaviors-delivered are hard axes; uiux_audit_test derives the docs document set from docs-site's own tables (a hand-written dozen had called the docs map dead in-process).

  9. Not done, named: app.itonami.cloud itself (network-awai/cloud-itonami, kotoba-ui + legacy HIG layer) is untouched — its tokens became the default, it was not moved onto cloud-kotoba-dds.theme. cloud-kotoba-dds.menu (the parallel session's pointer/context menu with its own runtime) overlaps jp-go-dds.behavior's menu and is not folded. The docs' :nav-one-home finding (docs map and sidebar both link /, quickstart, billing-and-usage; 82 documents at 0.25) is an IA decision. The composer of contracts.edn stays a chat.cljk view + browser script, not promoted. /billing/ overflows the 390 viewport by 24px on the live site before and after this session (the .kc-billing grid track resolves to 402px) — account-browser's billing block names it.")
  (:adr/body
  "## Verification, as run (main shas, not branch shas)

  - jp-go-dds nbb suite (kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test:../html/src:../css/src:../text/src test/run_tests.cljk): 58 tests / 1984 assertions / 0 failures at 4a315c5. Real browser (test/behavior_browser_test.cljk, chrome channel, 390 + 1280): 80 assertions — focus lands in the dialog and returns to the opener, Tab stays inside the modal, ArrowDown opens the menu and Escape returns, tabs on arrows with one panel visible and no navigation, combobox filters and Enter fills the hidden input, toasts leave / stay at 0, radiogroup arrows choose. `kbb -M:test` (the JVM parity gate) does not run under the kbb engine on main either (git deps unresolved) — unchanged.
  - shinkansen npm test: 119 tests / 389 assertions / 0 failures at b1ac87a; the strip-opaque test fails on the previous source (2 assertions).
  - cloud-kotoba-dds cljk suites at 80ad97b: theme 4/39, shell 2/17, switch 3/21, bots_workspace 3/36, interaction_components 5/50, all 0 failures; node test/shell.mjs at 390 / 1440 (rail unmoved — the first run moved it 48px, the focus-scroll fixed in jp-go-dds 4a315c5); examples/bots-workspace.html re-scored 100.0 with the behavior layer shipped (89.8 without: :chrome-layers and :behaviors-delivered named it).
  - app-kotoba-cloud at 312f20bf: npm run build ok; audit:uiux exit 0 (426 documents, no HARD, overall 98.4; the legal / tokushoho pages had lost the float layer when shell css moved and are on the theme); test:worker ok (slash-less docs 301 pinned before any asset read); test:workerd ok; kbb -M:test 248 failures = origin/main's 248 before the branch (site-test's landing needles from the 2026-09-13 branding change; sousa's evidence-kind schema query) — none new, none fixed; account-browser: signed-out / signed-in / account-menu / theme (dark by click, light by ArrowLeft, dark survives navigation) / secure / models blocks pass, the billing block fails on the pre-existing 390px overflow.
  - Live after deploy ae503a4f (curl + Chrome): /css/site.css declares 128 --hig-* (itonami's 117 minus kotoba.cloud's set = ∅), chrome-css / the float rule / the --ck aliases present; /js/theme.js 216 B, shinkansen.js 4145, behavior.js 17495, shell.js 581, switch.js 482; /account carries data-behavior=menu and =radiogroup; on /models/ at 1440 the body is rgb(242,242,242) at 17px / 22px, clicking dark sets data-theme=dark and stores it, ArrowLeft chooses light through the radiogroup, no page error. docs.kotoba.cloud/graph/: 57 classes with 3 rule-less hooks (the same three every healthy page has), docs map + shell top bar, light dark; /graph, /reference/quickstart, /integrations without the slash → 301 to the host form.

  ## Landed (merge sha on main)

  kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud 4639f5cb (#259), 312f20bf (#271); kotoba-lang/shinkansen d1a3ca3 (#4), 8029db9 (#6), b1ac87a (#7); kotoba-lang/jp-go-digital-design-system 9fd79a8 (#10), 4a315c5 (#11); kotoba-lang/cloud-kotoba-dds 80ad97b (#19). west pins: app-kotoba-cloud b5223631 → 4639f5cb, c68ba3bc → 312f20bf; jp-go-dds / shinkansen / cloud-kotoba-dds were advanced past these shas by parallel sessions the same day (4a315c5 / 301e50d / af6169d — each contains this session's merges).

  ## Resume point

  First command if continuing: cd orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud && npm run build && ACCOUNT_WAIT_MS=40000 kbb --backend sci test/account-browser.cljk — the billing block's 390px overflow is the first open item (find the .kc-billing child whose min-content is 402px; every child of the grid stretches to it). Then, in priority: fold cloud-kotoba-dds.menu onto jp-go-dds.behavior's menu (one runtime for a floating list); move network-awai/cloud-itonami's bots app onto cloud-kotoba-dds.theme (the owner's 'itonami の token を既定に' is satisfied at the token layer, the host is still on kotoba-ui); the docs :nav-one-home IA (82 documents); the composer as a component.

  ## Owner WIP preserved, not touched

  Superproject root: .gitignore modified and the untracked orgs/ directories reported by the SessionStart hook (not this session's). orgs/kotoba-lang/amu and orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang tracked changes reported by the hook. ~70 worktrees of other sessions under ~/.gftd/worktrees, /private/tmp/acc-autosync, ~/github/akc-pr2 and elsewhere (git worktree list on app-kotoba-cloud). Every worktree this session made (wt-shinkansen, wt-akc, wt-dds, wt-sk, wt-ckd, wt-akc2 in the session scratchpad; the root docs worktree for this ADR) is removed and its branch deleted locally and remotely. The shared checkouts of the four repos were fast-forwarded to their west pins by west update --fetch smart; none was dirty.")
))
